direction: down
title: "RESEARCH DEPENDENCIES, NOT AN IMPLEMENTATION PLAN\nLearn OCaml mechanisms; preserve Gambit's Scheme and C strengths"
title.shape: text
facts: "Exact current source and profile evidence\nExisting SMP / parallel STW collector / continuations\nKeep loaded-runtime and source capability separate"
meaning: "Preserved semantic domain and explicit contracts\nExecution / memory model / roots / control / FFI\nActual producer and lifetime closure"
c: "Full modern-C realization and retirement map\nSeparate worker / context / carrier / GC work state\nOne generated semantic plan; retained C capabilities"
gc: "GC choice and cost proof\nNursery sharing / promotion / all barriers and roots\nEliminated graph scans vs added work / memory / pauses"
effects: "Effects and continuation proof\nDelimitation / one-shot / multi-shot / dynamic-wind\nParallel task / native-resource / cancellation boundaries"
compiler: "Native compiler and service boundary\nHostGraph / FrameSpec / PointId / pass legality\nIndependent LLVM / MLIR products and invalidation"
increment: "Optional selected C-to-Zig hypothesis\nWhich owner is replaced? Which support really disappears?\nWhat C contract remains? What new costs enter?"
future: "Separate future acceptance\nSource argument != checked proof != native correctness\nCorrectness != measured net benefit\nAll current full gates remain unresolved"
